VERSION 1.1 AUGUST 7, 1994 by G-WiZ

--------------------
What this does..
--------------------

        If you'd like users of your CNet system to use your pfiles more
often, maybe you should advertise them! This simple AREXX program will
randomly display the title screens of your favorite pfiles during one point
in your sys.welcome. This version works for CNet 3.xx (tested only on CNet
3.05c PRO but should work on most others; if not just leave me email).

-------------------
Installation..
-------------------

Pretty simple (up to a point)!

1. Copy PScreen.rexx to your pfiles: directory

2. Make a directory where you will keep all the screens to be shown (default
   is SYSTEXT:PScreens/) .. the program WON'T do it for you!

3. Copy the main title screens of all your favorite pfiles into this new
   directory. Load them into an editor and add a banner to each one, telling
   the user that the game is now playing. For example:

(add something like) -->  - - - Play it now! It's in Pfiles! - - -
                          _____ _   _      _   
                         / ____| \ | |    | |  
  (existing             | |    |  \| | ___| |_ 
 pfile screen)          | |    | . ` |/ _ \ __|
                        | |____| |\  |  __/ |_ 
                         \_____|_| \_|\___|\__|
 __  __            _        _   _  __               _           _   
|  \/  |          | |      | | | |/ /              | |         | |  
| \  / | ___  _ __| |_ __ _| | | ' / ___  _ __ ___ | |__   __ _| |_ 
| |\/| |/ _ \| '__| __/ _` | | |  < / _ \| '_ ` _ \| '_ \ / _` | __|
| |  | | (_) | |  | || (_| | | | . \ (_) | | | | | | |_) | (_| | |_ 
|_|  |_|\___/|_|   \__\__,_|_| |_|\_\___/|_| |_| |_|_.__/ \__,_|\__|
                                                                    
4. You get the idea.. don't just put the screen or else they'll think they're
   playing it! Anyway save the screen as PScreen.x where x=1,2,3, etc. For
   example PScreen.1, PScreen.2, etc. When you're done adding screens to the
   directory, edit the PScreen.rexx pfile. CHANGE the MAX variable to how
   many screens are in the directory. I have nine screens that I want shown
   so MAX=9. Get it? Make sure that the 'path' variable is set to where you
   are keeping the screens in. The more screens you have, the better chances
   there are for each one to be displayed, since the randomizer is choosing
   between 1 and MAX.

5. Edit your SYSTEXT:sys.welcome file. Somewhere in there add this line:

\f1{#0pfiles:PScreen.rexx}

   where the { = ctrl-q and \ = ctrl-y (IMPORTANT!).

Okay that's it! Simple, eh? The hardest part is just copying the title
screens of games and adding a banner or whatever. I had to dig into some
programs and cut the main screens out. ANSI ones -- I just used a text editor
to put the banner on the top or bottom.

This program is CALLMEWARE.. it's free, just keep all the files together and
don't sell it without calling me first or I'll find you and bonk you on the
head. Call the BBS and look for more great stuff!

